
## 4. Five-level credibility — 24 scenarios

Rule table, evaluated in this order, first match wins:

| rule | level | predicate (all conjuncts required) |
|---|---|---|
| R0 | Unknown | actor identity `Ambiguous` — (pid,starttime) collided |
| R1 | Unknown | no process identity, and the only link is a shared session_id |
| R2 | Unknown | a file event exists and lies outside the actor's interval |
| R3 | Confirmed | keyed actor AND (self-observed OR fork edge) AND inside interval AND path tied to the command |
| R4 | Strong | >= 2 independent source classes AND >= 1 kernel-observed |
| R5 | Probable | keyed actor AND (self-observed OR fork edge) AND inside interval AND NO file evidence tied to the command |
| R6 | Weak | inside the interval and nothing more |
| R7 | Unknown | residual |

Independence is defined, not felt: classes differ AND neither source is marked
derived AND the pair is in INDEPENDENT_PAIRS (declared/proc, declared/fs,
proc/fs). Two hooks firing twice are ONE source.

| # | scenario | expected | rule | actual | rule | verdict |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| S01 | actor itself is the reported writer, path tied, inside interval | Confirmed | R3 direct fork evidence, inside interval | Confirmed | R3 direct fork evidence, inside interval | PASS |
| S02 | one-hop fork chain, path tied, inside interval | Confirmed | R3 direct fork evidence, inside interval | Confirmed | R3 direct fork evidence, inside interval | PASS |
| S03 | four-hop fork chain (pipeline), path tied | Confirmed | R3 direct fork evidence, inside interval | Confirmed | R3 direct fork evidence, inside interval | PASS |
| S04 | (pid,starttime) collision, everything else perfect | Unknown | R0 (pid,starttime) collision | Unknown | R0 (pid,starttime) collision | PASS |
| S05 | collision plus two independent corroborations | Unknown | R0 (pid,starttime) collision | Unknown | R0 (pid,starttime) collision | PASS |
| S06 | only a shared session_id | Unknown | R1 session identity only | Unknown | R1 session identity only | PASS |
| S07 | no actor at all, file event present | Unknown | R1 session identity only | Unknown | R1 session identity only | PASS |
| S08 | file event strictly outside the actor's interval | Unknown | R2 no overlapping time window | Unknown | R2 no overlapping time window | PASS |
| S09 | declared hook + kernel fs agree, path tied, no fork chain | Strong | R4 two independent sources, same fact | Strong | R4 two independent sources, same fact | PASS |
| S10 | declared hook + kernel proc agree, no file evidence | Strong | R4 two independent sources, same fact | Strong | R4 two independent sources, same fact | PASS |
| S11 | kernel proc + kernel fs agree | Strong | R4 two independent sources, same fact | Strong | R4 two independent sources, same fact | PASS |
| S12 | two declared shells report the same command (hook fired twice) | Weak | R6 time-window overlap only | Weak | R6 time-window overlap only | PASS |
| S13 | kernel fs claim marked derived from kernel proc | Weak | R6 time-window overlap only | Weak | R6 time-window overlap only | PASS |
| S14 | fork chain inside interval, no filesystem evidence at all | Probable | R5 pid chain inside window, no file-side evidence | Probable | R5 pid chain inside window, no file-side evidence | PASS |
| S15 | fork chain inside interval, untied path observed | Probable | R5 pid chain inside window, no file-side evidence | Probable | R5 pid chain inside window, no file-side evidence | PASS |
| S16 | actor is the reported writer, but path untied | Probable | R5 pid chain inside window, no file-side evidence | Probable | R5 pid chain inside window, no file-side evidence | PASS |
| S17 | pid-only actor with a tied path inside the interval | Weak | R6 time-window overlap only | Weak | R6 time-window overlap only | PASS |
| S18 | pid-only actor, pid equality, no window overlap | Unknown | R7 residual (nothing to stand on) | Unknown | R7 residual (nothing to stand on) | PASS |
| S19 | keyed actor, no lineage, untied path, inside interval | Weak | R6 time-window overlap only | Weak | R6 time-window overlap only | PASS |
| S20 | keyed actor, no file event, no lineage, inside interval | Weak | R6 time-window overlap only | Weak | R6 time-window overlap only | PASS |
| S21 | three independent classes (declared + proc + fs) | Strong | R4 two independent sources, same fact | Strong | R4 two independent sources, same fact | PASS |
