| S23 | keyed actor, tied path, no time containment recorded | Unknown | R2 no overlapping time window | Unknown | R2 no overlapping time window | PASS |
| S24 | one kernel source corroborating only itself | Weak | R6 time-window overlap only | Weak | R6 time-window overlap only | PASS |

24/24 scenarios match the specified level AND rule.

### 4.0 Why each scenario sits where it does

| # | scenario | note |
|---|---|---|
| S01 | actor itself is the reported writer, path tied, inside interval | same-source direct evidence |
| S02 | one-hop fork chain, path tied, inside interval | kernel-reported parent edge |
| S03 | four-hop fork chain (pipeline), path tied | depth does not weaken a real edge |
| S04 | (pid,starttime) collision, everything else perfect | collision detected -> refuse |
| S05 | collision plus two independent corroborations | more evidence cannot outvote a broken identity |
| S06 | only a shared session_id | session is not attribution |
| S07 | no actor at all, file event present | 0-E: inotify carries no pid |
| S08 | file event strictly outside the actor's interval | temporal impossibility |
| S09 | declared hook + kernel fs agree, path tied, no fork chain | two independent classes, one kernel |
| S10 | declared hook + kernel proc agree, no file evidence | kernel proc corroborates the command itself |
| S11 | kernel proc + kernel fs agree | two kernel sources, still not Confirmed |
| S12 | two declared shells report the same command (hook fired twice) | same class twice is one source, not two |
| S13 | kernel fs claim marked derived from kernel proc | independence is per-source, not assumed from class alone |
| S14 | fork chain inside interval, no filesystem evidence at all | the canonical 'probably, but unproven' case |
| S15 | fork chain inside interval, untied path observed | a path nobody tied to the command does not confirm it |
| S16 | actor is the reported writer, but path untied | writer identity strong, artefact link weak |
| S17 | pid-only actor with a tied path inside the interval | missing starttime removes the identity, keeps the interval |
| S18 | pid-only actor, pid equality, no window overlap | nothing holds |
| S19 | keyed actor, no lineage, untied path, inside interval | time overlap only |
| S20 | keyed actor, no file event, no lineage, inside interval | still only time |
| S21 | three independent classes (declared + proc + fs) | three sources still cap at Strong without a fork edge |
| S22 | inferred-only corroboration, fork chain otherwise perfect | inferred inputs are filtered from R4, not from R3 |
| S23 | keyed actor, tied path, no time containment recorded | unknown containment is treated as no containment |
| S24 | one kernel source corroborating only itself | a single source is never 'two independent sources' |

### 4.1 Level distribution over the 24 scenarios

| level | count |
|---|---|
| Confirmed | 4 |
| Strong | 4 |
| Probable | 3 |
| Weak | 6 |
| Unknown | 7 |

### 4.2 Monotonicity: adding a corroboration never lowers the level

violations: 0 (must be 0)
